    "caption": "Test prep shouldn't be a privilege.\n\nThe SAT prep industry is broken.\n\nFor many families, it's financially out of reach. With a private tutor costing $50-150 per hour and many prep courses priced in the hundreds or thousands, access to quality SAT preparation is a privilege, not a right.\n\nMoreover, one-size-fits-all courses don't cut it. Each student has unique needs, yet generic programs waste time covering what students already know, resulting in inefficient study time.\n\nThe result? The best prep methods remain in the hands of those who can afford it, leaving many students behind.\n\nEnter PrepifyMe: a 100% free, adaptive, AI-powered Digital-SAT prep platform. It offers per-skill practice targeting precisely what students get wrong, backed by AI-matched difficulty and gamified retention. Every student deserves tailored, high-quality prep that doesn’t empty their wallet.\n\nPrepifyMe is the smart, free play that redefines SAT prep accessibility.\n\nPrepifyMe is live, and free, at prepifyme.com.\n\n#EdTech #AI #satprep #educationinnovation",
